# What lies in `inner` comes through a table of listeners: both classes may lie there. Two names are asked of it; one allocated class has both. The names asked choose what is expected, not what is proven.
# The store is in a helper, so the field is appended. A store directly behind Object.create() is a field of a constructed object, whose classes are proven.
